      "label": "User projected onto the children playing in water",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the children playing in water, as the meme's intent relies on the viewer identifying with or observing the children being mislabeled as 'sea monkeys'. The projection is implicit, not explicit (e.g., no 'me' or 'you'), but the viewer is positioned as the observer of the scene and the subject of the stereotype being applied. The user is projected onto the scene and the visual material within it.",
