      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_06afd5d6",
      "@type": "TargetCommunity",
      "instance_name": "audience_id",
      "label": "audience description",
      "description": "The target audience for this meme is individuals who are familiar with or find humor in racially charged stereotypes, particularly those that exoticize or dehumanize people with dark skin tones by labeling them as 'sea monkeys.' The meme relies on the audience's recognition of the derogatory stereotype and their ability to perceive the absurdity or irony in the mislabeling, even if it is offensive. The audience may include internet users who engage with absurdist or edgy humor, often found in meme culture, and who may not be aware of or insensitive to the harmful racial implications of the stereotype. The meme's intent to provoke laughter through visual-textual juxtaposition targets those who find humor in the juxtaposition of children playing in water with the offensive label 'sea monkeys,' despite the potential for harm.",
